### 5.1.4 Routing Threshold Sweep Results

A post-hoc routing threshold sweep was performed over ten candidate values of p* ∈ {0.50, 0.55, ..., 0.95} on the validation set without any model retraining. The results are summarised in Table 5.3.

**[Table 5.3 — Routing Threshold Sweep Results (Distilled MobileCount)]**

| p* | System MAE | System RMSE | Sparse MAE (≤100) | % to MobileCount |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0.50 (argmax) | 182.45 | 764.0 | 33.6 | 66.6% |
| 0.70 | 181.58 | 763.8 | 29.6 | 65.0% |
| 0.75 | 180.93 | 763.6 | 27.4 | 63.8% |
| **0.85** | **180.92** | **763.6** | 27.7 | **63.0%** |
| 0.90 | 185.05 | 766.3 | 27.4 | 61.2% |

The optimal threshold p* = 0.85 produces the minimum system MAE of 180.9. The system exhibits low sensitivity to threshold choice in the range p* ∈ [0.70, 0.85] (MAE variation < 1.0 point), identifying a stable operating region. Beyond p* = 0.85, the excess routing of dense-boundary images to LCDNet incurs accuracy penalties that outweigh the sparse-scene improvement.

---

