## 5.3 Final Design Adjustments

Based on the performance evaluation conducted in Section 5.1 and the analysis of design solutions in Section 5.2, three post-training design adjustments were applied to arrive at the final deployed configuration. None of these adjustments required retraining any model component.

**Adjustment 1 — Calibrated Routing Threshold (p* = 0.85):**
The default routing policy, which routes to MobileCount when P(dense) > P(sparse) (i.e., p* = 0.50), was replaced with a calibrated threshold of p* = 0.85 following the exhaustive post-training sweep described in Section 5.1.4. This adjustment reduces system MAE from 182.4 to 180.9 — a 1.5-point improvement at zero additional cost. The adjustment was motivated by analysis of the router's confidence distribution: the majority of routing errors occur for images in the 65–95% confidence range, where the scene density is genuinely near the routing boundary. Setting p* = 0.85 requires the router to be highly confident before dispatching an image to MobileCount, reducing boundary-region misrouting.

**Adjustment 2 — Exclusion of Soft Fusion:**
Soft fusion — which blends the density map outputs of both specialists weighted by router confidence — was evaluated across the full range of fusion weights (α ∈ [0.0, 1.0] in steps of 0.1). No setting produced a MAE below the hard-routing optimum. The additional complexity and marginal latency increase of soft fusion (-56 ms vs. ~55 ms for hard routing) provide no compensating accuracy benefit. Soft fusion is therefore excluded from the final configuration, simplifying the inference pipeline.

**Adjustment 3 — Deployment of Distilled Dense Specialist:**
The baseline MobileCount checkpoint (MAE 213.2) was replaced by the knowledge-distilled checkpoint (MAE 198.7) in the final deployed pipeline. This substitution reduces system MAE from 183.0 to 180.9 with no change to the deployed parameter count (0.884M), GFLOPs (1.07), or GPU latency (3.4 ms). The distillation phase (12 epochs, ~4 hours on RTX 3050) represents the only additional training cost.

